15 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating three different gas sampling methods. \(A\) Manual sampling: Transfer of samples from chambers to vials, then shipped to the lab for GC analysis. \(B\) Portable TGA: Direct sampling from chambers to a TGA device placed by six chambers. \(C\) Multi-valve system: Direct sampling from chambers to a valve unit connected to a pump and TGA, managed by a laptop, installed in a car near the chambers.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Flowchart illustrating three sampling methods over a 30-minute timeline: \(A\) Manual sampling with six points; \(B\) Portable TGA with individual points at intervals; \(C\) Multi-valve system with simultaneous sampling of three groups of points. Each method shows different sampling sequences labeled A1, C1, A2, C2, A3, C3.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Charts display CH4 concentration over time for two systems: Portable TGA and Multi-valve. Step 2 shows graphs A and B, while Step 3 shows graphs C and D. Graphs A and C are for Portable TGA, showing slopes of 28.49 and 8.86 ppb/sec. Graphs B and D are for Multi-valve, with slopes 15.33 and 7.81 ppb/sec. Each graph includes trend lines and R-squared values to indicate fit quality. Time in seconds is on the x-axis, and CH4 concentration in ppb is on the y-axis.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt <> /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 51 0 R /Alt (Line graphs showing methane emission rates \(milligrams per square meter per day\) at 8:00 a.m. and 10:00 a.m. The graphs compare AWD and CF treatments across various measurement methods: GC, Portable, and Multi-valve, identified with different colored lines and symbols. Emission rates are displayed for treatments AWD1, AWD2, AWD3, CF1, CF2, and CF3 under conditions labeled W1 and W2. Emission rates vary, with noticeable differences between 8:00 a.m. and 10:00 a.m.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 52 0 R /Alt <> /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 53 0 R /Alt (Comparison of manual and laser-based chamber approaches using radar charts. Chart A \(Manual chamber\) shows moderate strength in affordability and simplicity, but lower in detection accuracy and velocity of screening. Chart B \(Laser-based chamber\) compares a portable TGA and a multi-valve system. The multi-valve system has a higher velocity of screening, while the portable TGA excels in mobility and affordability. Legend indicates rating scale from one to five, with five indicating strength.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 41 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
